In June 2021, the City Council enacted an ordinance establishing the Urban Renewal
Authority (URA) and passed a resolution identifying blighted areas within the community.
The URA, consisting of a five-member board with expertise in community planning, urban
renewal, and business management, is tasked with reviewing Urban Renewal Plans and
Projects for designated areas. The board also provides recommendations on the use of
Tax Increment Financing (TIF) to support these initiatives.
